            {
              "line": 76,
              "type": "agentMessage",
              "id": "msg_070ee88d8b68f728016a9f6fddf7d487d2b84503c784ea4d3c",
              "text": "I\u2019m using the `webmcp-tool-authoring` skill because you explicitly approved authoring a bounded WebMCP capability. I\u2019ll first read its instructions and inspect the repository/app structure and existing Complete operation, then I\u2019ll report the required changes without editing anything.",
              "phase": "commentary",
              "memoryCitation": null,
              "delivery": null,
              "questions": null,
              "turnId": "01a07ecc-e67e-70a0-b6aa-48858b158c01"
            },
            {
              "line": 177,
              "type": "agentMessage",
              "id": "msg_070ee88d8b68f728016a9f6ff1343887d2a829bdfd26bc424e",
              "text": "The skill requires a single product-facing tool, reuse of the existing domain function, bounded input validation, lifecycle/cancellation handling, fixed safe errors, and a repository-native contract test. I\u2019m now locating the app entry points, repository-local instructions, and any existing WebMCP/domain implementation so the proposed change is grounded in the actual code.",
              "phase": "commentary",
              "memoryCitation": null,
              "delivery": null,
              "questions": null,
              "turnId": "01a07ecc-e67e-70a0-b6aa-48858b158c01"
            },
            {
              "line": 534,
              "type": "agentMessage",
              "id": "msg_070ee88d8b68f728016a9f700ffff887d28a9d4d50386f9418",
              "text": "Inspected the app and skill guidance. No files were changed.\n\nCurrent structure:\n\n- `domain.mjs` already provides cancellable `completeTask(id, { signal })`.\n- `ui.mjs` already preserves the dependency boundary via `mountTools(modelContext)`.\n- `webmcp.mjs` is currently a no-op and needs the implementation.\n- Existing tests cover only the visible Complete button.\n- Baseline: `npm test` passes.\n\nThe implementation should:\n\n1. Register exactly one `complete_task` WebMCP tool through `modelContext.registerTool`.\n2. Accept only `{ taskId }`, as a string of 1\u201380 characters, with no coercion or extra properties.\n3. Match the schema and runtime validation.\n4. Call the supplied `completeTask` exactly once per accepted execution and forward cancellation.\n5. Return a fixed, input-independent success acknowledgement.\n6. Use fixed safe errors for validation, cancellation, registration, and domain failures.\n7. Provide an idempotent disposer that aborts registration, cancels pending work, and invalidates retained callbacks.\n8. Ensure cancellation before mutation prevents completion; uncertain post-commit cancellation must not report success or retry.\n9. Add repository-native contract tests covering registration, validation, success, visible/domain/audit state, cancellation, disposal, and failure behavior.\n\n`domain.mjs` and the existing `ui.mjs` mount boundary should remain unchanged. Send your next message when you want me to implement this.",
              "phase": "final_answer",
